- `APPINSTANCEGROUP`: app instance group.

If you specify other values, the error code `InvalidResourceType.Invalid` is returned.

This parameter is required.', example='APPINSTANCEGROUP'),
  tag?: [ 
    {
      key?: string(name='Key', description='The tag key. This parameter is required. The tag key must be 1 to 128 characters in length and is case-sensitive. It cannot start with `aliyun` or `acs:` (case-insensitive) and cannot contain `http://` or `https://`. It supports letters, digits, spaces, and common Chinese and English punctuation marks. If the tag key does not meet the rules, the error code `InvalidTagPolicy.KeyInvalid` is returned.

This parameter is required.', example='Resolution'),
      value?: string(name='Value', description='The tag value. This parameter is required. The tag value must be 0 to 256 characters in length and is case-sensitive. Empty strings are allowed. It cannot contain `http://` or `https://`. If the tag value does not meet the rules, the error code `InvalidTagPolicy.ValueInvalid` is returned.

If the tag key is a system tag, the tag value can only be `true` or `false`.

This parameter is required.', example='720p', nullable=false),
    }
  ](name='Tag', description='The list of tags to bind. This parameter is required. You can specify up to 20 tags in a single request. You must specify both Key and Value for each tag.

- Tag keys in the same request cannot be duplicate. Otherwise, the error code `InvalidTag.Duplicated` is returned.
- If a tag with the same key already exists on the resource, the tag value is updated to the value specified in the current request.
- A single resource can be bound to up to 20 custom tags. If this limit is exceeded, the error code `ResourceTag.CustomTagCountExceed` is returned.

Tag keys starting with `System/` are Wuying system tags. Only the following values are supported, and the tag value can only be `true` or `false`:

- `System/Scheduler/GRAYSCALE`: the canary release tag for the app instance group.
- `System/Scheduler/STOP_NEW_USER_CONNECTION`: prevents newly bound users from establishing connections to the app instance group.

